# 🔵 Level 3 – OAuth 2.0 & OpenID Connect

## OAuth 2.0

OAuth allows one application to access another service **without sharing your password**.

Example:

```text
Login with Google
```

or

```text
Login with GitHub
```

The application receives permission without learning your password.

---

## OpenID Connect (OIDC)

OIDC builds on OAuth 2.0 and adds **identity verification**.

OAuth = Authorization

OIDC = Authentication + Authorization

---

# Access Control Models

## RBAC (Role-Based Access Control)

Permissions depend on role.

Example:

```text
Admin

↓

Manage Users

↓

Employee

↓

View Own Profile
```

---

## ABAC (Attribute-Based Access Control)

Permissions depend on attributes.

Examples:

* Department
* Location
* Time
* Device
* Clearance level

Example:

Finance employee

AND

Office network

AND

Business hours

↓

Access Granted

---

# Zero Trust Authentication

Traditional model:

```text
Login Once

↓

Trust Forever
```

---

Zero Trust:

```text
Verify

↓

Monitor

↓

Verify Again

↓

Continuous Validation
```

Every access request is evaluated.

---

# 🌍 Real-World Example

An employee logs into Microsoft 365.

The system checks:

✔ Password

✔ MFA

✔ Device compliance

✔ Location

✔ Risk score

If something changes unexpectedly (for example, a login from another country), additional verification may be required.

